> ### Name: design_crossed
> ### Title: Create a Balanced Crossed, Between-Within, or Testlet
> ###   Experimental Design
> ### Aliases: design_crossed
> 
> ### ** Examples
> 
> des <- design_crossed(
+   factors = list(
+     exposure = c("incidental", "intentional"),
+     spacing  = c("massed", "distributed")
+   ),
+   allocation = "latin_square",
+   contrast   = "sum",
+   attrition  = 0.05
+ )
> print(des)

── glmmplanr Experimental Design ──

• Factors (2): exposure (incidental, intentional) [within-participant,
within-item] x spacing (massed, distributed) [within-participant, within-item]
• Allocation: "latin_square" (4 cells; each participant sees each item once; 4
lists rotate within-pair conditions)
• Cell names for `cell_probs`: "incidental_massed", "incidental_distributed",
"intentional_massed", and "intentional_distributed"
• Balanced sample-size multiples: n_subj = 4k, n_item = 4m
• Factor coding: "sum" | Trial missingness: 5% | Participant dropout: 0%
• Fixed formula: `~exposure * spacing`
• Subject RE: `~exposure * spacing` | Item RE: `~exposure * spacing`
> 
> 
