> ### Name: report_plan
> ### Title: Write a Sample Size Justification
> ### Aliases: report_plan
> 
> ### ** Examples
> 
> # Create the five-replication demonstration plan from the optimizer help.
> example("optimize_sample_size", package = "glmmplanr", local = environment(), echo = FALSE)
> report_plan(plan, print_output = FALSE)
[1] "### Sample Size Justification\n\nNo evaluated design has confirmed attainment within constraints. The candidate is 16 participants x 8 items (indeterminate, 5 replications). Target-scale power was 60.0% [23.1%, 88.2%], and mean accuracy difference interval width was 32.16 percentage points (1.475 logit). Final verification covered 2 of 2 lattice points. Primary analysis: bayes_laplace, intercept_only random effects, logit link. Target uncertainty: coefficient standard error. The target interval level was 95%. Stage-2 Wilson intervals are pointwise across 2 verified decisions without simultaneous multiplicity adjustment. Target attainment status reflects only the specified power/precision targets and does not verify inferential validity (Stage-2 H1 coverage was 80.0% (95% Wilson CI 37.6% to 96.4%); null Type I error was not evaluated). Confirm interval coverage and Type I error in independent simulations at the selected design with validate_design_point(). Required attainment was 80%."
> 
> 
> 
